      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Spruce_Hill%2C_Philadelphia",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "Two Market‑Frankford Line stations—40th Street and 46th Street—serve Spruce Hill, keeping the neighborhood connected to downtown.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        25
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Spruce_Hill%2C_Philadelphia",
      "category": "transport",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "Clark Park houses a rare 1890 Charles Dickens statue by Francis Edwin Elwell, one of only two in the U.S.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        8,
